            <ArticleTitle>[67 year old man with abdominal pain, anorexia and low-grade fever].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>287-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of pericardial effusion presenting clinically with pretamponade is shown. TBC is not a rare cause of Pericardial effusion and at present Tuberculosis is a more and more frequent infection also in occidental countries. Guide lines for diagnosis and treatment are revised.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
